You're not allowed to sell food in non-metric units.  You must display
the metric price most prominently, but may display prices using Imperial
units for comparison purposes.

In Germany, the German words meaning "one pound" mean "500 grams".

In England, the English words "one pound" mean "one Imperial pound".

Mercifully, we're still allowed to sell beer in good honest Imperial
pints.  Preferably in pint-to-line, not pint-to-brim, glasses.

